{"description":"The universal capture gateway emits drafts that can never publish. Every reconciled draft in the live workspace lacks a `dimension` field, so `eka draft validate` refuses with a blocking R6 error and `eka publish` can never succeed. Confirmed on seven drafts (bug:fix-reconciled-changes-anvil-a2a6, ...get, ...readme, spec:spec-reconciled-spec-anvil, ...spec-content, ...spec-render-execution, and others). Two further defects compound it: (a) `classifyGitHeuristic` derives the artifact type by substring-matching the joined file list, which includes snapshot transport paths such as `exchange/snapshots/units/eka/dec-.../unit.json`, so a scratch change under `cmd/` can be classified `spec-` because of a snapshot filename - the same transport-noise class already fixed for the code graph but never applied here; (b) the below-threshold branch assigns `confidence = threshold - 0.05`, which is still below the threshold, then clamps to 0.4, so the documented 'created but flagged low' state is unreachable arithmetic.","impact":"A headline v1.10 capability produces a permanent backlog of unpublishable files instead of knowledge, and the backlog pollutes `eka publish --all` for unrelated work. Root cause: the git-reconcile classifier lives only in `eka-cli/cmd/capture.go` and never routes selection through `runtime.CaptureService.Evaluate`, although ADR-035 places the gateway in eka-core. Fix: set a valid dimension for every knowledge token, exclude transport directories from the inspected file list, make type selection independent of snapshot filenames, correct or delete the contradictory confidence branch, and move selection into core so one implementation serves both the git and prompt paths. Regression test: a captured draft for each supported token must validate without a blocking finding."}